# ~/.claude version control — ALLOWLIST model: ignore everything, then
# un-ignore only the config/code layer. This is leak-proof against new data
# dirs (transcripts, dream data, .turn-state, telemetry, caches) that a
# blocklist would silently start tracking.
#
# Raw data (projects/, assets/, widgets/, plugins/, sessions*/, .turn-state/,
# output/, telemetry/, …) is NOT tracked — it moves via rsync per
# mac-migration/MANIFEST.md §6. Standalone sub-projects become their own repos
# (see PORTABILITY.md). Secrets are never tracked.
#
# The learned-state dirs (subconscious/, i-dream/, pinned/, memory-domain/,
# personas/) are DIFFERENT and are deliberately tracked, un-ignored below, then
# carved back at the bottom of this file. The rule is: keep the curated insight,
# drop the queues, cursors and derivations. This paragraph used to list them as
# untracked, which contradicted the un-ignore lines twenty rows down and sent at
# least one session hunting for a bug that was a stale comment.

# 1) ignore everything by default
/*
.*

# 2) un-ignore the config/code layer
!/.gitignore
!/PORTABILITY.md
!/*.md
!/settings.json
!/mcp-catalog.json
!/scripts/
!/skills/
# skills-parked/: the 11 skills moved out of the roster by mig 0048. Kept in
# the repo, just not loaded — so it needs its own un-ignore line, because the
# allowlist above ignores every new top level by default (owner ruling
# 2026-08-20, after a sync nearly recorded the move as 428 bare deletions).
!/skills-parked/
!/hinters/
!/rules/
!/git-hooks/
!/conventions/
!/features/
!/personas/
!/migrations/
!/hooks-feedback-domain/
# style/: config layer tracked; thesaurus.jsonl (data ledger) + derived/
# (machine-written digests) travel by rsync like every other ledger (mig 0033)
!/style/
/style/*
!/style/scope-map.json
!/style/glossary-hints.tsv

# accumulated LEARNED state — real value, version it (all tiny unless noted)
!/memory/
!/i-dream/
!/pinned/
!/sessions-domain/
!/memory-domain/
!/subconscious/

# 3) re-exclude scratch + data + transient INSIDE the allowlisted areas
# Unanchored on purpose: a leading slash would pin this to the repo root, and
# scratch checkpoints are written wherever a session is working (scripts/kanban/,
# skills/<name>/). 14 of them reached the repo that way before this was widened.
_*.claude.md
/wal.md
/wal.jsonl
/weekly-todos.md
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.venv/
**/locks/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
*.log
.DS_Store
hooks-feedback-domain/events.jsonl
hooks-feedback-domain/derived/
hooks-feedback-domain/dream/cursor.json
hooks-feedback-domain/dream/insights.jsonl
hooks-feedback-domain/dream/.adapter-seen
**/_seen.json

# subconscious: keep CURATED outputs (patterns/insights/intentions/valence/
# calibration), drop the 130M of raw churn (logs, raw samples, traces, chains)
subconscious/logs/
subconscious/crash-reports/
subconscious/metacog/samples.jsonl
subconscious/dreams/traces/
subconscious/dreams/snapshots/
subconscious/introspection/chains/
# domain runtime pointers (regenerated)
sessions-domain/dream/cursor.json
memory-domain/dream/cursor.json

# Three kinds of churn that were tracked by accident, untracked 2026-08-16.
# They fit the carve-out principle already above (keep curated insight, drop
# raw churn) and were simply never added, so ~65 files reappeared in every
# git status and buried the config layer.
#
#   queues      transient by definition; a queue's contents are never a record
#   cursors     position files, meaningless outside the run that wrote them
#   derived     regenerable from the inputs, which ARE tracked
#
# All still live on disk and still travel by rsync per mac-migration
# MANIFEST.md §6. Nothing is lost, it stops being versioned.
# Owner ruling 2026-08-16: the goal is a good-enough backup of the gcc without
# dragging along large logs or intermediate state already captured in refined
# form. Queues, cursors and derivations go; curated insight stays.
#
# Left TRACKED for now, though the same test arguably catches them:
# subconscious/metacog/audits/ (2.3M, 320 files) and dreams/project-briefs/
# (412K, 94 files). No code reads either — every reference is a transcript, WAL
# or shell log — and their refined forms (metacog/calibration.jsonl,
# metacog/activity.jsonl, dreams/insights.md, dreams/patterns.json) are tracked.
# Untracking them is a one-line change here plus a git rm --cached.
subconscious/dreams/ingest-queue/
i-dream/derived/
subconscious/dreams/yield-state.json
subconscious/dreams/reinforce-state.json
subconscious/dreams/processed.json
subconscious/dreams/digest-meta.json
subconscious/metacog/processed.json
subconscious/state.json
